---
// The quickstart block is the README's, verbatim.
---

<section class="install" id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Up in one command.</h2>
      <p>
        Docker on amd64 or arm64. The compose file brings TimescaleDB with it. You add an admin password, a free
        MaxMind GeoLite2 key, and the path to your proxy's log file.
      </p>
      <p>
        Without the key it still starts, in geo-degraded mode, and tells you what is missing. The only traffic it sends
        out is the GeoLite2 download and, unless you turn it off, one public-IP lookup for the map's home. No
        telemetry.
      </p>
      <p class="links">
        <a href="/docs/get-started/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
        <a href="/docs/sources/nginx/">Log formats</a>
        <a href="/docs/sources/proxy-setup/">Behind a CDN or tunnel</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre class="block"><code>mkdir geometrikks &amp;&amp; cd geometrikks
curl -LO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GilbN/geometrikks/main/docker-compose.yml
curl -Lo .env https://raw.githubusercontent.com/GilbN/geometrikks/main/.env.example
$EDITOR .env   <span class="c"># APP_ADMIN_PASSWORD, MaxMind key, log path</span>
docker compose up -d
<span class="c"># open http://localhost:8000</span></code></pre>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .install {
    padding: 100px 0 120px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .install .wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .install p {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .links a {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .install {
      padding: 64px 0;
    }
    .install .wrap {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
